More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (711–720)
711. Improper Validation of Session Expiration
Session Expiration Bypass
Sessions remain active even after timeout limits, allowing attackers to continue using them.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
712. Insecure Handling of OAuth Access Tokens
OAuth Access Token Leakage
OAuth tokens are exposed through logs, URLs, or browser storage.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
713. Improper Validation of Payment Confirmation APIs
Payment Confirmation Manipulation
Attackers manipulate payment confirmation endpoints to falsely validate transactions.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $15,000
714. Insecure Handling of File Preview Features
File Preview Injection
File preview systems execute malicious scripts embedded in uploaded files.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
715. Improper Validation of User Group Permissions
User Group Privilege Escalation
Attackers escalate privileges by manipulating group membership.
💰 Typical payout: $700 – $12,000
716. Insecure Handling of Temporary Download Links
Temporary Download Link Reuse
Temporary links remain valid longer than intended and can be reused.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
717. Improper Validation of Comment Systems
Comment System Injection
Comment sections allow injection of malicious scripts or code.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
718. Insecure Handling of API Versioning
Deprecated API Exposure
Old API versions remain accessible and contain vulnerabilities.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
719. Improper Validation of File Conversion Services
File Conversion Service Exploit
File conversion tools execute malicious payloads embedded in uploaded files.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
720. Insecure Handling of Application Debug Endpoints
Debug Endpoint Exposure
Debug endpoints reveal stack traces, environment variables, or internal configuration.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
